 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "yoma.6a.4",
   "daf": "6a",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "מַפְרִישִׁין כֹּהֵן גָּדוֹל וְכוּ׳. לָמָּה מַפְרִישִׁין? לָמָּה מַפְרִישִׁין?! כִּדְקָאָמְרִינַן, אִי לְרַבִּי יוֹחָנָן כִּדְאִית לֵיהּ, אִי לְרֵישׁ לָקִישׁ כִּדְאִית לֵיהּ!",
   "en": "§ After a long digression in which many peripheral issues were addressed, the Gemara returns to interpreting the mishna. It was taught in the mishna: The Sages would «remove the High Priest» from his house to the Chamber of Parhedrin. The Gemara asks: «Why do» the Sages «remove him?» The Gemara asks in astonishment: «Why do» the Sages «remove him?» It is «as we stated above: Whether» it is according «to Rabbi Yoḥanan, as per his» opinion: Sequestering of the High Priest is derived from the sequestering prior to the inauguration; «or whether it is» according «to Reish Lakish, as per his» opinion: Sequestering of the High Priest is derived from sequestering at Sinai, the answer is clear. What is the point of the Gemara’s question?"
  }
 ],
